<title>SINGAPORE: Noble debuts 18 pct above IPO price.</title>
<headline>Noble debuts 18 pct above IPO price.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Hong Kong-based Noble Group debuted on Friday at a high of US$1.04, a premium of 18 percent over its initial public offer price of US$0.88 each.  </p>
<p>After 25 minutes of trade, Noble was trading at US$1.01 on 4.44 million units.</p>
<p>Noble markets, process and transports industrial and agricultural materials.</p>
<p>It had offered a total of 51 million shares, of which 41.19 million were placed out. Its public offer was 18.8 times subscribed.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
